   "text": "This SMILES is my reading of the drawing. Its stereocentres come from my own wedge/hash analysis of the 2D layout, and I did not cross-check them against a CIP assignment or a reference structure.\n\n**Regions of the structure**\n- **Cyclohexane ring:** it carries a hashed OH, a wedged OMe and a wedged link to the vinyl group.\n- **Trisubstituted alkene:** it joins the cyclohexane to the macrocycle. The cyclohexyl and the methyl sit on the same side of the double bond, so the cyclohexyl and the ester-bearing CH are trans.\n- **Macrocycle:** it contains the ester O\u2013C(=O) to a pipecolate (piperidine-2-carboxylate), whose nitrogen is acylated by the C(=O)C(=O) unit.\n- **Pyranose hemiketal:** a six-membered ring bearing OH, a CH(CH3), an OMe and the ring oxygen.\n- **Remaining macrocycle chain:** three OMe-bearing CH carbons, a trisubstituted trans alkene with a methyl, a ketone, a CH(OH) and a CH(CH3).\n- **Side chain:** a CH bearing \u2013CH2CH2CH2\u2013S\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH2.\n\n**Closing the macrocycle:** the ring closes at the CH(CH3) bonded to the ester-bearing CH, written in the SMILES as the ring-closure pair labelled 4.\n\nSMILES: O[C@@H]1CC[C@H](C[C@H]1OC)/C=C(C)/[C@H]4OC(=O)[C@@H]2CCCCN2C(=O)C(=O)[C@]3(O)O[C@@H]([C@@H](OC)C[C@H]3C)[C@@H](OC)C[C@@H](OC)C/C(C)=C/[C@H](CCCSCCN)C(=O)C[C@H](O)[C@H]4C"
